## Physical models guiding the chord progressions
A model for the path of chord progression allows to compute variables over time, with retroaction
- the model gives a prediction of value, can be used over windows of different size, so it can be used for dynamic generation
- it needs to be combined with heuristics (structural patterns such as cycle of fifth exploration or scale degrees, or random) that destabilize the equilibrium
- the meta-parameters are
    - the parameters of the physical model according to some dimensions
    - as well as the parameters of the heuristics

### Spring
[text](https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syst%C3%A8me_masse-ressort)
- One-dimensional stable point
- Force applied -> callback force
- Oscillation around a stable point

Examples :
0 -> 1 -> 0 = crashing on the lower limit
0 -> 1 -> -1 -> 0 = no lower limit
0 -> 2 -> 1 -> 0 = crashing on the lower limit
0 -> 2 -> 0 = strong callback force
=> The spring does not seem a good approximation for the chord progression when there is a lower limit.
