### Gravity, stability
[text](https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%89quation_d%27orbite)
- Orbit : rotation around a center
- Disturbances -> less stable -> can change (tonal?) center
- Unstable orbit -> getting farther away or spiral
- Crashing movement

### Pendulum
[text](https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pendule_simple)
- Constant oscillation => moving equilibrium
- Force accumulates by itself with oscillations, from first impulsion
- First impulsion can be stronger, then it will fall to the equilibrium


| I need systems that apply forces, and systems that resolve forces.
| These systems combine themselves sequentially.
| The forces are applied and resolved relative to different windows of context
| Example : up the scale -> IV -> V -> I
| Example : up the scale -> IV -> further away bVII -> IV -> I
| Example : up the scale -> III -> V/III -> III -> up the scale -> V -> I



## Time series
- Take a metric over a chord progression
- Model it as a time series (ARMA for instance)
- Predict the next, originality = probability
- The meta parameters are the parameters of the model as well as the fitness of the chord progression to the model

## Simple statistics
- Have constraints on start and ending chord
- Compute the mean, std, skewness etc of
- the chord progressions are ranked according to these statistics
- the meta-parameters influence the weight of the statistics => re-ranking









